```

**Responsive Breakpoints Summary:**

| Breakpoint | Filter Behavior |
|-----------|-----------------|
| Mobile (< md) | Always-visible filters inline, collapsible filters in drawer behind button |
| Desktop (>= md) | All filters inline, no drawer needed |
| Drawer Height | 85vh max height with scrollable content |

```
★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────
The architecture elegantly separates concerns: (1) **URL-first persistence** stores filters in search params (not component state), enabling bookmarking and sharing, while localStorage acts as a fallback for auto-load on fresh visits. (2) **Responsive abstraction** through ResponsiveFilterBar encapsulates the mobile/desktop decision (drawer vs. inline) while components remain agnostic to layout. (3) **One-shot skip flag** prevents re-applying cleared filters—this is a subtle but important UX pattern avoiding the "cleared filters magically come back" problem. The hook-based active filter counting creates reactive badges without prop drilling.
