```
In CI environments, events flush every 1ms to avoid hanging; in production, it uses LaunchDarkly's default behavior.

**Graceful Shutdown Sequence** (feature-flags.service.ts:52-65):
```typescript
async onApplicationShutdown(signal?: string | undefined): Promise<void> {
  if (this.client) {
    try {
      await this.client.flush();  // Line 54: Flush pending events
    } catch (e) {
      this.logger.warn(`Failed to flush LaunchDarkly events during shutdown: ${String(e)}`);
    }
    try {
      await this.client.close();  // Line 59: Close the connection
    } catch (e) {
      this.logger.warn(`Failed to close LaunchDarkly client during shutdown: ${String(e)}`);
    }
    this.client = null;  // Line 63: Clear reference
    this.isInitialized = false;  // Line 64: Reset state
  }
}
```

The shutdown handler ensures: (1) pending events are flushed before connection closes (line 54), (2) both flush and close operations have independent try-catch blocks to prevent one failure from preventing the other (lines 53-62), and (3) client state is cleaned up to prevent reuse after shutdown (lines 63-64).
